+# Flash Sale — DDD Design Spec
+
+> **Status:** design / conceive layer
+> **Date:** 2026-06-13
+> **Author:** DDD strategic modeling pass
+> **Playbooks read:** `.claude/skills/ddd-spec/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/ddd-modeling/SKILL.md`,
+> `CLAUDE.md §"Modeling from another system"`, `.specs/2026-05-26-audit-distillation-what-we-got-wrong.md` (RC-1, RC-2, RC-3, RC-6, RC-12)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Requirements
+
+### 1.1 Problem Overview
+
+Merchants need to run time-boxed promotional campaigns ("flash sales") that discount a chosen
+set of catalog products for a short, defined window. The storefront displays a live countdown
+so shoppers know how long the deal lasts. The sale ends automatically when the window closes;
+for sales with a hard cap, it can also end early once the capped quantity sells out.
+
+### 1.2 Functional Requirements
+
+**Flash Sale Authoring (Merchant)**
+- Merchant creates a flash sale with a name, a `SaleWindow` (start + end datetimes), and one
+  or more `DiscountLine`s (product reference + discount + optional per-line cap).
+- Merchant may add or remove product lines while the sale is in `DRAFT` status.
+- Merchant may set an optional global cap (`globalCapQuantity`) — a ceiling on total units sold
+  across all lines in the sale.
+- Merchant schedules the sale (transitions `DRAFT → SCHEDULED`).
+- Merchant may cancel a `DRAFT` or `SCHEDULED` sale.
+
+**Automatic Lifecycle**
+- Sale activates automatically when `window.startsAt` is reached
+  (`SCHEDULED → ACTIVE`).
+- Sale ends automatically when `window.endsAt` is reached (`ACTIVE → ENDED`,
+  reason `WINDOW_CLOSED`).
+- If `globalCapQuantity` is set and the aggregate's `soldQuantity` reaches it,
+  the sale ends early (`ACTIVE → ENDED`, reason `CAP_REACHED`).
+
+**Storefront Display**
+- Storefront shows discounted prices for products that belong to an `ACTIVE` flash sale.
+- Storefront shows a countdown (`remainingSeconds`) for `SCHEDULED` and `ACTIVE` sales.
+- If a cap is configured, storefront may show remaining available quantity.
+
+**Attribution & Cap Enforcement**
+- When an order item is confirmed in the ordering context and was attributed to a flash sale,
+  the flash sale's `soldQuantity` is incremented.
+- If the increment crosses `globalCapQuantity`, the aggregate ends the sale and raises
+  `FlashSaleEnded` (reason `CAP_REACHED`).
+
+### 1.3 Non-Functional Requirements
+
+- **Scheduler precision:** activation and expiry use case calls triggered by a scheduler;
+  ≤ 30 s drift is acceptable for the storefront experience.
+- **Cap race safety:** `soldQuantity` increments inside a `UnitOfWork` transaction; the
+  aggregate enforces the cap check and raises the end event atomically with the save.
+- **Storefront read:** countdown and price display are read concerns — eventual consistency
+  (poll ~5 s or SSE) is acceptable.
+- **Tenant isolation:** every flash sale is scoped to a `storeId`; cross-store reads are not
+  permitted.
+- **Immutability after activation:** a sale's lines and window cannot be changed once
+  `ACTIVE`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Candidate Concepts — Question Every Aggregate
+
+Each noun the brief implies is evaluated against the decision tree from CLAUDE.md §"Question
+Every Aggregate". The default is the **leanest option**; a concept becomes an aggregate only
+when identity + lifecycle + invariants + confirmed need are all present.
+
+| Candidate | Classification | Justification |
+|---|---|---|
+| **FlashSale** | **AGGREGATE** | Has identity (UUID), a four-state lifecycle (`DRAFT → SCHEDULED → ACTIVE → ENDED\|CANCELLED`), multiple enforced invariants (≥1 line before scheduling, valid window, positive cap, transition guards), and is the confirmed core need of the feature. |
+| **DiscountLine** | **VALUE OBJECT** (embedded collection on FlashSale) | Exists only within a FlashSale; no independent lifecycle or identity. Mutated solely through FlashSale methods. Modeled as a plain embedded struct. |
+| **SaleWindow** | **VALUE OBJECT** (embedded on FlashSale) | A `startsAt`/`endsAt` date pair — defined entirely by value. Invariant (`endsAt > startsAt`) is enforced by the VO itself on construction. No identity. |
+| **Discount** | **VALUE OBJECT** (discriminated union, embedded in DiscountLine) | A percentage reduction (in basis points) or a fixed monetary reduction — defined by value. Two structurally distinct shapes; modeled as a discriminated union, never an optional-field bag. No identity. |
+| **Storefront countdown** | **QueryService / BFF read** | `remainingSeconds` is `window.endsAt − now`, computable from the projection. No write-side model needed. Adding a "countdown entity" would be RC-2 over-modeling. |
+| **soldQuantity tracker** | **Field on FlashSale aggregate** (not a separate aggregate) | Cap enforcement is a write-side invariant that the FlashSale aggregate must guard in the same transaction as the increment. A separate `SoldQuantityTracker` entity with its own repository would create a two-aggregate consistency hazard and would be RC-2 over-modeling. `soldQuantity: number` lives on the aggregate root. |
+| **CatalogProduct** | **Cross-context reference by ID** (catalog context owns it) | FlashSale references products by `productId`. The catalog context is upstream — the flash-sale context never holds a reference to the full product object, only the ID. No entity here. |
+| **Activation / expiry scheduler** | **Domain service + scheduled job** | A `FlashSaleSchedulerService` (or Go worker) queries sales in `SCHEDULED` state whose `window.startsAt ≤ now` and triggers the `ActivateFlashSale` use case; similarly for `EndFlashSale`. Not an aggregate — no persistent state of its own. |
+| **FlashSaleParticipation** (order attribution record) | **NOT MODELED** | The `flashSaleId` stamped on an `OrderLine` in the ordering context is sufficient traceability. A separate participation entity here would be RC-2 over-modeling ("a thing that happened" is already captured by the `FlashSaleItemSold` integration event). |
+| **Audit log table** | **NOT MODELED** | Domain events (`FlashSaleCreated`, `FlashSaleScheduled`, etc.) persisted in the outbox/`domainEvent` table are the audit trail. A dedicated audit table is RC-2 over-modeling. |
+| **Analytics / reporting context** | **DEFERRED** (see §8) | Not confirmed in the brief. Scope discipline: do not build. |
+| **Notifications context** | **DEFERRED** (see §8) | Not in the brief. |
+| **Coupon codes** | **DEFERRED** (see §8) | A distinct discount mechanism; not in this brief. |
+
+---
+
+## 3. Bounded Contexts
+
+One bounded context captures the confirmed need. The feature is cohesive and small (one
+aggregate, five use cases, two published integration events); splitting further would be RC-2
+over-engineering with no lifecycle or team-ownership justification.
+
+---
+
+### BC1: `flash-sale` — **Core**
+
+**Responsibility:** Owns the full lifecycle of merchant-configured, time-boxed discount
+campaigns — authoring, scheduling, activation, cap enforcement, and expiry.
+
+**Ubiquitous Language:** FlashSale, SaleWindow, Discount, DiscountLine, globalCapQuantity,
+soldQuantity, FlashSaleStatus.
+
+**Aggregates:**
+
+- `FlashSale` (root) — see §4 for full lifecycle and invariants
+  - `window: SaleWindow` — embedded VO
+  - `lines: DiscountLine[]` — embedded VO collection
+  - `globalCapQuantity: number | null` — optional cap field
+  - `soldQuantity: number` — mutable cap counter
+
+**Cross-context references (by ID only):**
+- `storeId: string` — tenant identifier; owned by the `auth`/`store` context
+- `productId: string` per `DiscountLine` — owned by the `catalog` context
+
+**Upstream contexts (consumed):**
+- `ordering` context — publishes `ordering.flashSaleItemSold` integration event (carries
+  `flashSaleId`, `quantity`) → handled by `RecordSaleAttributionHandler` in this context.
+
+**Downstream consumers:**
+- `catalog` / storefront — consumes `flash-sale.flashSaleActivated` and
+  `flash-sale.flashSaleEnded` integration events to update displayed prices.
+
+**Published integration events:**
+- `flash-sale.flashSaleActivated`
+- `flash-sale.flashSaleEnded`
+
+---
+
+**Context map:**
+
+```
+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│             flash-sale  (Core)                       │
+│                                                      │
+│  FlashSale ─── SaleWindow (VO)                       │
+│             ─── DiscountLine[] (VO)                  │
+│                  └── Discount (VO, discriminated)    │
+└──────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+       │  references by ID                  ▲ integration events
+       │                                    │ flashSaleActivated
+       ▼                                    │ flashSaleEnded
+┌──────────────┐        flashSaleItemSold  │
+│  catalog     │    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  (upstream   │    │  ordering  (upstream, C/S)  │
+│   supplier)  │    │                             │
+│  productId   │    │  stamps flashSaleId on       │
+│  read-only   │    │  OrderLine; publishes        │
+└──────────────┘    │  flashSaleItemSold event     │
+                    └─────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+Relationship types:
+- `catalog → flash-sale`: **Customer-Supplier** — flash-sale consumes product IDs supplied by catalog.
+- `ordering → flash-sale`: **Customer-Supplier** — flash-sale receives attribution events from ordering.
+- `flash-sale → catalog/storefront`: **Open Host Service / Published Language** — flash-sale publishes integration events that downstream contexts conform to.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Aggregates & Invariants
+
+### FlashSale
+
+**Lifecycle:**
+
+```
+DRAFT
+  │  schedule()  — must have ≥1 line; window valid; endsAt must be after now
+  ▼
+SCHEDULED
+  │  activate()  — triggered by scheduler at window.startsAt
+  ▼
+ACTIVE
+  │  end(reason) — triggered by scheduler at window.endsAt (WINDOW_CLOSED)
+  │               OR by recordSale() when soldQuantity reaches cap (CAP_REACHED)
+  ▼
+ENDED
+
+From DRAFT or SCHEDULED:
+  │  cancel()
+  ▼
+CANCELLED
+```
+
+**Fields:**
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | `FlashSaleId` | UUID v7 |
+| `storeId` | `string` | Tenant scope |
+| `name` | `string` | min 1 char, max 120 chars |
+| `status` | `FlashSaleStatus` | Lifecycle phase |
+| `window` | `SaleWindow` | VO: `{ startsAt, endsAt }` |
+| `lines` | `DiscountLine[]` | min 1 when scheduling |
+| `globalCapQuantity` | `number \| null` | null = unlimited; integer > 0 if set |
+| `soldQuantity` | `number` | starts at 0; never decremented |
+
+**Value Objects (nested):**
+
+`SaleWindow`
+- `startsAt: Date`
+- `endsAt: Date`
+- Invariant: `endsAt > startsAt` (enforced in VO constructor)
+- Invariant: duration ≥ 1 minute
+
+`Discount` (discriminated union — never collapsed into an optional-field bag):
+- `{ kind: "PERCENTAGE"; basisPoints: number }` — basisPoints ∈ (0, 10000]
+- `{ kind: "FIXED"; amountCents: number; currency: string }` — amountCents > 0
+
+`DiscountLine`
+- `productId: string` — catalog cross-reference by ID
+- `discount: Discount`
+- `capQuantity: number | null` — per-line cap; null = unlimited; integer > 0 if set
+
+**Invariants enforced by the aggregate:**
+
+| # | Invariant | Error code |
+|---|---|---|
+| I-1 | `schedule()` requires `lines.length ≥ 1` | `FLASH_SALE_NO_LINES` |
+| I-2 | `schedule()` requires `window.endsAt > now` | `FLASH_SALE_WINDOW_ALREADY_PASSED` |
+| I-3 | `activate()` only when `status = SCHEDULED` | `FLASH_SALE_NOT_SCHEDULED` |
+| I-4 | `end()` only when `status = ACTIVE` | `FLASH_SALE_NOT_ACTIVE` |
+| I-5 | `cancel()` only when `status ∈ {DRAFT, SCHEDULED}` | `FLASH_SALE_CANNOT_CANCEL` |
+| I-6 | `addLine()` / `removeLine()` only when `status = DRAFT` | `FLASH_SALE_ALREADY_SCHEDULED` |
+| I-7 | `globalCapQuantity > 0` if provided | `FLASH_SALE_INVALID_CAP` |
+| I-8 | `recordSale(qty)` only when `status = ACTIVE` | `FLASH_SALE_NOT_ACTIVE` |
+| I-9 | Duplicate `productId` across lines is not allowed | `FLASH_SALE_DUPLICATE_PRODUCT` |
+
+**Methods and domain events raised:**
+
+| Method | Transition | Domain Event(s) raised |
+|---|---|---|
+| `create(...)` (static factory) | → `DRAFT` | `FlashSaleCreated` |
+| `addLine(line)` | stays `DRAFT` | — |
+| `removeLine(productId)` | stays `DRAFT` | — |
+| `schedule()` | `DRAFT → SCHEDULED` | `FlashSaleScheduled` |
+| `activate()` | `SCHEDULED → ACTIVE` | `FlashSaleActivated` |
+| `end(reason)` | `ACTIVE → ENDED` | `FlashSaleEnded` |
+| `cancel()` | `DRAFT\|SCHEDULED → CANCELLED` | `FlashSaleCancelled` |
+| `recordSale(qty)` | stays `ACTIVE` (or triggers `end()` if cap hit) | `FlashSaleSoldQuantityUpdated`; conditionally `FlashSaleEnded` |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Domain & Integration Events
+
+### Domain Events (raised by FlashSale aggregate; persisted in outbox/domainEvent table)
+
+| Event | Raised by | Payload (key fields) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `FlashSaleCreated` | `create()` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `name`, `window`, `lines` |
+| `FlashSaleScheduled` | `schedule()` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `window` |
+| `FlashSaleActivated` | `activate()` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `window`, `lines` |
+| `FlashSaleEnded` | `end(reason)` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `reason: FlashSaleEndReason`, `soldQuantity` |
+| `FlashSaleCancelled` | `cancel()` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId` |
+| `FlashSaleSoldQuantityUpdated` | `recordSale(qty)` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `soldQuantity` |
+
+### Internal Handler Reactions
+
+- `FlashSaleActivated` → `InternalHandler` publishes integration event
+  `flash-sale.flashSaleActivated` to cross-context bus.
+- `FlashSaleEnded` → `InternalHandler` publishes integration event
+  `flash-sale.flashSaleEnded` to cross-context bus.
+
+### Integration Events
+
+**Published (flash-sale → downstream):**
+
+| Integration Event | Payload | Consumed by |
+|---|---|---|
+| `flash-sale.flashSaleActivated` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `window`, `lines: { productId, discount }[]` | catalog / storefront — to display discounted prices and countdown |
+| `flash-sale.flashSaleEnded` | `flashSaleId`, `storeId`, `reason: FlashSaleEndReason`, `endedAt` | catalog / storefront — to clear discounts |
+
+**Consumed (ordering → flash-sale):**
+
+| Integration Event | Payload | Handled by |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ordering.flashSaleItemSold` | `flashSaleId`, `orderId`, `quantity` | `RecordSaleAttributionHandler` → calls `RecordSaleAttribution` use case → `flashSale.recordSale(qty)` |
+
+### Use Cases (command-side)
+
+| Use Case | Actor / Trigger | Key aggregate method |
+|---|---|---|
+| `CreateFlashSale` | Merchant | `FlashSale.create(...)` |
+| `AddDiscountLine` | Merchant | `flashSale.addLine(line)` |
+| `RemoveDiscountLine` | Merchant | `flashSale.removeLine(productId)` |
+| `ScheduleFlashSale` | Merchant | `flashSale.schedule()` |
+| `CancelFlashSale` | Merchant | `flashSale.cancel()` |
+| `ActivateFlashSale` | Scheduler (at `window.startsAt`) | `flashSale.activate()` |
+| `EndFlashSale` | Scheduler (at `window.endsAt`) | `flashSale.end("WINDOW_CLOSED")` |
+| `RecordSaleAttribution` | Handler (on `ordering.flashSaleItemSold`) | `flashSale.recordSale(qty)` |
+
+### Query Use Cases (read-side — BFF, no entity load)
+
+| Query | Screen / Caller | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ListFlashSales` | Merchant dashboard | Paginated; filter by status |
+| `GetFlashSale` | Merchant detail view | Full lines + soldQuantity |
+| `GetActiveFlashSaleForProduct` | Storefront | Returns discount + countdown for a productId; `null` if no active sale |
+
+---
+
+## 6. Contract Lock (Phase 0)
+
+These enums and integration events must be **frozen in `packages/contracts`** (TypeSpec source)
+before any bounded-context implementation begins. Freezing them first enables `flash-sale` and
+`ordering` contexts to be built in parallel without serializing through the contracts file
+(RC-9 / CLAUDE.md §Phase 0).
+
+### Enums
+
+```typescript
+// packages/contracts/src/flash-sale/enums.tsp
+
+enum FlashSaleStatus {
+  DRAFT,
+  SCHEDULED,
+  ACTIVE,
+  ENDED,
+  CANCELLED,
+}
+
+enum DiscountKind {
+  PERCENTAGE,   // reduction expressed in basis points (100 bp = 1%)
+  FIXED,        // reduction expressed as amountCents + currency
+}
+
+enum FlashSaleEndReason {
+  WINDOW_CLOSED,   // normal expiry at window.endsAt
+  CAP_REACHED,     // optional global cap hit before window.endsAt
+}
+```
+
+### Integration Events (TypeSpec)
+
+```typescript
+// packages/contracts/src/flash-sale/events.tsp
+
+// Published by flash-sale context
+model FlashSaleActivatedEvent {
+  name: "flash-sale.flashSaleActivated";
+  payload: {
+    flashSaleId: string;
+    storeId: string;
+    activatedAt: utcDateTime;
+    window: { startsAt: utcDateTime; endsAt: utcDateTime; };
+    lines: Array<{
+      productId: string;
+      discount:
+        | { kind: DiscountKind.PERCENTAGE; basisPoints: int32; }
+        | { kind: DiscountKind.FIXED;      amountCents: int64; currency: string; };
+      capQuantity: int32 | null;
+    }>;
+  };
+}
+
+model FlashSaleEndedEvent {
+  name: "flash-sale.flashSaleEnded";
+  payload: {
+    flashSaleId: string;
+    storeId: string;
+    endedAt: utcDateTime;
+    reason: FlashSaleEndReason;
+    soldQuantity: int32;
+  };
+}
+
+// Published by ordering context, consumed here
+// (ordering context owns this definition; listed here for cross-context awareness)
+model FlashSaleItemSoldEvent {
+  name: "ordering.flashSaleItemSold";
+  payload: {
+    flashSaleId: string;
+    orderId: string;
+    quantity: int32;
+  };
+}
+```
+
+### Per-language bindings
+
+Run once after TypeSpec authoring, before BC work:
+
+```bash
+bun sdk          # regenerates @template/contracts-typescript + @template/contracts-go
+```
+
+Both contexts (`flash-sale` TS backend, any future Go worker) import from the generated
+bindings — never hand-roll their own event shapes.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Ubiquitous Language Glossary
+
+Canonical spellings to use consistently everywhere in the codebase (identifiers, event names,
+error codes, prose, comments, API fields). A single naming-harmonization pass was applied
+before writing this spec (RC-12).
+
+| Term | Canonical form | Rejected alternatives |
+|---|---|---|
+| **FlashSale** | `FlashSale` / `flashSale` | "promotion", "deal", "campaign", "sale event", "time sale" |
+| **SaleWindow** | `SaleWindow` / `window` | "period", "duration", "interval", "timeframe", "schedule" |
+| **Discount** | `Discount` / `discount` | "markdown", "reduction", "offer", "promo rate" |
+| **DiscountLine** | `DiscountLine` / `line` (within the flash-sale context) | "item", "product entry", "sale product", "promotion line" |
+| **status** | `status` | "externalStatus", "saleState", "phase" |
+
+---
+
+## 8. Out of scope / deferred (not modeled)
+
+The following were considered and explicitly deferred — not silently dropped — because the
+brief does not confirm them. Each must be re-evaluated before work begins if the scope
+expands.
+
+| Concept | Reason for deferral |
+|---|---|
+| Analytics / reporting context (revenue per sale, conversion) | Not confirmed in the brief. Scope discipline: build only on confirmed requirements. |
+| Notifications to shoppers (email, push, SMS) | Not in the brief. Would be a separate context consuming `flash-sale.flashSaleActivated`. |
+| Coupon codes | A structurally different discount mechanism with its own redemption lifecycle. Distinct feature. |
+| Loyalty / reward points tied to flash purchases | Not mentioned. |
+| Customer-facing "my flash-sale purchases" history | An ordering-context read concern, not a flash-sale domain responsibility. |
+| Multi-currency discount normalization | `FIXED` discount VO carries `currency`; cross-currency conversion logic is not modeled here. |
+| Per-customer purchase limits (e.g. "max 2 per customer") | Not in brief. Would add a `customerPurchaseRecord` concept. |
+| Flash sale templates / recurring sales | Not in brief. Would extend the lifecycle. |
+| Admin audit log table | Domain events in the outbox/`domainEvent` table are the audit trail (RC-2). |
+| Per-line sold-quantity cap enforcement at the aggregate | The VO carries `capQuantity` per line (data is modeled), but the write-side enforcement logic across concurrent orders on a per-line basis is deferred until the ordering context can emit per-line attribution events. Global cap enforcement is in scope. |
